SUMMARY:Curator's Talk | The Art of Paper
DESCRIPTION:Join us as Susan Gosin and Cynthia Nourse Thompson\, two of the three curators of The Art of Paper\, will discuss the fascinating realization of this exhibition\, which features works by acclaimed artists from the 20th and 21st centuries drawn from the extensive collection of Jordan D. Schnitzer and his Family Foundation.  \nHighlights include the evolution of handmade paper art as a progression from and response to the historic relationship between print and paper\, revealing another important story about the act of collaboration among artists\, fine printers\, and hand papermakers at renowned publishing studios.  \nSusan Gosin grew up as a member of five generations of commercial papermakers in Wisconsin. After receiving her MFA at the University of Wisconsin\, Madison\, she cofounded Dieu Donné in New York City in 1976. She has been involved in the field of hand papermaking as an artist\, educator\, writer\, lecturer\, and collaborator for fifty years. Her work has been exhibited and collected by institutions such as MoMA\, New York; the Metropolitan Museum of Art\, New York; and the Getty\, Los Angeles.   \nCynthia Nourse Thompson is currently Professor and Director of Curatorial Affairs at the Zuckerman Museum of Art at Kennesaw State University. Prior to this position\, for six years she was Associate Professor and Director of the graduate programs in Book Arts & Printmaking and Studio Art at University of the Arts in Philadelphia\, PA\, while also serving as curator for the Joy Pratt Markham Gallery at the Walton Arts Center in Fayetteville\, AR. As a curator\, Thompson has organized and curated more than 50 exhibitions since 2000. \nArturo Herrera\, Mine\, 2007\, pigmented abaca watermark on pigmented cotton base sheet with hand-cut collaged\npulp painting\, edition 9/23\, 60 x 30 inches. © Arturo Herrera\, Collection of Jordan D. Schnitzer.
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/curators-talk-the-art-of-paper/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:In Conversation
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/2008.139-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
